{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Call now, if there is any that will answer thee; and to which of the saints wilt thou turn?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For wrath killeth the foolish man, and envy slayeth the silly one.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have seen the foolish taking root: but suddenly I cursed his habitation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His children are far from safety, and they are crushed in the gate, neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " any to deliver ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whose harvest the hungry eateth up, and taketh it even out of the thorns, and the robber swalloweth up their substance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Although affliction cometh not forth from the dust, neither doth trouble spring out of the ground;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet man is born to trouble, as the sparks fly upward.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would seek to God, and to God would I commit my cause:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who doeth great things and unsearchable; wonderful things without number:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who giveth rain upon the earth, and sendeth waters upon the fields:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To set on high those that are low: that those who mourn may be exalted to safety.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He disappointeth the devices of the crafty, so that their hands cannot perform ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " enterprise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He taketh the wise in their own craftiness: and the counsel of the froward is carried headlong.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They meet with darkness in the day-time, and grope in the noon-day as in the night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he saveth the poor from the sword, from their mouth, and from the hand of the mighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the poor hath hope, and iniquity stoppeth her mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, happy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the man whom God correcteth: therefore despise not thou the chastening of the Almighty:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he maketh sore, and bindeth up: he woundeth, and his hands make whole.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He will deliver thee in six troubles: yea, in seven there shall no evil touch thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In famine he will redeem thee from death: and in war from the power of the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt be hid from the scourge of the tongue: neither shalt thou be afraid of destruction when it cometh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At destruction and famine thou shalt laugh: neither shalt thou be afraid of the beasts of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou shalt be in league with the stones of the field: and the beasts of the field shall be at peace with thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt know that thy tabernacle ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in peace; and thou shalt visit thy habitation, and shalt not sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt know also that thy seed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great, and thy offspring as the grass of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt come to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " grave in a full age, as a shock of corn cometh in in its season.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.5.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.5.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo this, we have searched it, so it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; hear it, and know thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for thy good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
